WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.830
MARKUS KLUTE: All right.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.630
So welcome back to 8.701.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.250
So we have all ingredients
now to prepare Feynman rules

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.270
for QED.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.010
So that's the toolkit
we need in order

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:19.660
to make calculations to
calculate scattering processes

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.580
and decays.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.780
And we've already seen Feynman
rules for our toy theory.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.970
Again, now the situation
is a little bit more

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.860
complicated, because
we can consider

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.409
the spin of
particles in addition

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:35.140
to their energy and momentum.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.740
The rules' sequence of things
are very much the same.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.140
There is, however, a few
caveats to keep in mind,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.210
and I'll point those out.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:43.710
OK.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.570
So the very first thing is to
be very clear in our notation.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.610
So this is an arbitrary or
generic QED Feynman diagram.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.010
We have only pointed
out the incoming

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.900
and the outgoing lines.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.450
There is internal lines
which I didn't mention here.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:06.750
Important to note the
momentum and the directions.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.550
The directions are arbitrary.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.530
We just have to be
clear on them and then

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.476
treat them consistently.

00:01:12.476 --> 00:01:13.115
All right?

00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:16.800
So this is not different
in our previous discussion.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.190
Then, here comes the difference.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.040
Our external lines
either electron,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.820
positrons, or photons.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.320
All right?

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:30.790
You can-- fermions and photons,
charged fermions and photons.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.580
So we discussed how
the solutions look

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:39.710
like, our spinors u and v.
And for outgoing electrons,

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:43.710
for outgoing particles, we have
this adjunct vector here, which

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.560
is given by u dagger gamma 0.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.920
And similarly for the
incoming antiparticle--

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.530
v dagger gamma 0.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.800
For the photon, we have
the polarization vectors

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.730
for incoming and
outgoing photons.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.300
All right.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.830
Then we have a vertex factor.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:11.350
Here, now, g e is a constant
and a dimensionless property.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:15.710
But we do have to
have a gamma mu here

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.610
as part of our vertex factor.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.070
For the propagator,
our internal lines,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.400
we have a difference between
electrons, positrons,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.090
and photons.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.150
And that comes from the fact
that electrons and positrons

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.620
are massive particles.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.700
So we have vertex
vectors which now

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.610
have this 1 over
q square behavior,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.530
or 1 over q square
minus m square behavior.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:43.560
So here, you can
already see that there's

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.700
going to be a complication later
when we evaluate or integrate

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.180
over momentum--

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.730
simply the same
discussion I had before.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.450
And we already know how to
solve this problem of infinities

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:59.230
by renormalizing-- by having a
cut-off and renormalizing it.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:00.730
Excellent.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.920
So the next step, then,
is very much the same.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.180
There's no change.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.420
We have to make sure that
there's energy and momentum

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.075
conservation, and
we enforce this

00:03:09.075 --> 00:03:11.650
by introducing delta functions.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.800
We have to integrate over each
and every internal momenta,

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:22.600
and each internal line gets one
of those integration factors.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.910
And then after we integrate, we
are left with a delta function,

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.470
and we have to cancel
that delta function.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.580
All right.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.660
In our toy experiment, the
order of things didn't matter.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.770
Everything we had in there
was scalar numbers, right?

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:45.270
Here we do have a little bit
more complicated problem.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:48.240
So there's an
importance in the order

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.440
of which we execute things.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.640
So what we want to do
is form fermion lines.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.030
We just follow a fermion as we
go from the left to the right.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:00.690
And then we find things
which are always of the form

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:05.970
an adjoint spinor, a 4-times-4
matrix, and a spinor.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:09.060
And the result of that
is going to be a number.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:09.870
All right?

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:10.650
Great.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.990
There is one additional
complication,

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:16.350
is accounting for
duplications and making sure

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.720
that the sign is [INAUDIBLE].

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.230
I'm just mentioning this here.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.990
This will become more clear
as you work through examples.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.170
So there is an
antisymmetrization going on,

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.000
where we have to
introduce a minus

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.250
sign between different
diagrams that differ only

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.610
by the interchange or the
exchange of two incoming or two

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.900
outgoing electrons or positrons
and/or the incoming electron

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.500
with an outgoing positron.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.470
So if you have a diagram
which is exactly the same,

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.760
but the two incoming
electrons are interchanged,

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.800
you have to add
those two diagrams.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.190
You have to add all
matrix elements together

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.778
for recalculating amplitude.

00:04:55.778 --> 00:04:57.570
But you have to introduce
a minus sign when

00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:01.030
you change those two particles.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.470
So with that, we can now
just basically calculate

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.780
whatever QED process we want.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.880
All the tools are already here.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.715
And what we want to do now
next, in the next video,

00:05:11.715 --> 00:05:15.570
and also in the
recitation and homework,

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.460
is to go through a
few examples to get

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.470
a little practice with this.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.680
There's a number of tricks
which will come in handy,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.410
and I'll explain those
in a separate video.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.940
They are just
mathematical tricks

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.910
which allow us to
quickly evaluate

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:35.490
the multiplication of spinors
and matrix elements and so on.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.600
All right.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.340
That's it for this video.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.850
Again, there is going to
be another two or three

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:46.060
videos which deal with actually
evaluating or calculating

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.910
matrix elements.

